## How to Verify an East West Marquise Ring Before You Buy

Three checks every ring must pass before you commit.

**Check 1 — Confirm the finger length-to-width ratio is 2.0+ (or at minimum 1.5+).** Measure finger length base-to-tip. Measure finger width at the widest point. Divide. If below 1.5, pick a vertical marquise instead — east west will not flatter the finger shape.

**Check 2 — Confirm V-tip centre prongs at order.** East west does not reduce tip chip risk. V-tip prongs on the horizontal tips are mandatory. Most listings include this at $0 extra on upgrade.

**Check 3 — Confirm wedding band compatibility.** Pick straight band or pavé eternity. Avoid contour V-notch or chevron bands. [IGI](https://www.igi.org/) and [GIA 4Cs](https://4cs.gia.edu/) both certify loose stones only — the setting orientation is on the retailer's listing.

I run these three checks before I quote any client on an east west marquise ring. All three must pass for the ring to deliver on the horizontal-illusion promise.

